.TH RGBLED 1 "June 12, 2026"
.UC 4
.SH NAME
rgbled \- set the n64cart RGB LED brightness
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rgbled
[
.I red green blue
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rgbled
controls the n64cart RGB LED through
.IR /dev/rgbled0 .
When three arguments are supplied, they set the red, green, and blue channel
brightness values.  Each channel must be in the range 0 through 255.  Values
may be decimal or use the C
.B 0x
hexadecimal prefix.
.PP
With no arguments,
.B rgbled
prints the current red, green, and blue values.
.SH EXAMPLES
Set the LED to red:
.PP
.RS
.nf
rgbled 255 0 0
.fi
.RE
.PP
Turn the LED off:
.PP
.RS
.nf
rgbled 0 0 0
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP 12
.I /dev/rgbled0
n64cart RGB LED ioctl device
